      "message": "I was thinking if we should have an allowlist for this(like what we did for iommu registers). Reading the generic coreboot code, SMMSTORE and OPAL also passes an address in RBX, but chromebooks do not support those. From what I understand, we need to support only `APM_CNT_ACPI_ENABLE` and `APM_CNT_ACPI_DISABLE`. So probably something like:\n\n```\nswitch (val) {\n  case GSMI_CALLBACK:\n  \tpkvm_handle_gsmi(vcpu);\n  \tbreak;\n  case APM_CNT_ACPI_ENABLE:\n  case APM_CNT_ACPI_DISABLE:\n  \toutb(val, port);\n  \tbreak;\n  default:\n  \tkvm_inject_gp(vcpu, 0);\n  \treturn X86EMUL_UNHANDLEABLE;\n  }\n```\n\nWDYT?",
